WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:06.010 --> 00:07.130
Wow!

00:08.780 --> 00:10.400
So pretty.

00:10.400 --> 00:11.740
You're right!

00:15.260 --> 00:16.970
All right, let's take a break here.

00:17.390 --> 00:18.430
We should.

00:19.470 --> 00:20.790
Agreed!

00:21.120 --> 00:22.120
Everyone, come out!

00:30.030 --> 00:30.580
You guys too!

00:35.440 --> 00:36.510
Please come out!

00:41.240 --> 00:42.120
Come on out.

00:54.920 --> 00:56.640
It seems like they're having a good time.

00:57.960 --> 00:59.840
Don't go too far!

01:08.360 --> 01:09.370
I will make us some tea.

01:09.720 --> 01:10.630
I'll help you.

01:54.440 --> 02:00.130
Onbat and Floette!
An Encounter in the Wind!!

02:00.870 --> 02:05.950
As Satoshi and his friends continue their journey towards Eisetsu Gym to obtain the eighth badge,

02:01.080 --> 02:10.960
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:01.080 --> 02:10.960
Z

02:06.320 --> 02:08.510
they have taken a short break.

02:17.070 --> 02:17.820
Caught you!

02:18.130 --> 02:20.750
Squishy, I'll squish you!

02:21.220 --> 02:22.910
Squish-squish-squish!

02:23.590 --> 02:25.240
Nuzzle-nuzzle-nuzzle-nuzzle.

02:58.290 --> 02:59.110
That voice just now...

02:59.650 --> 03:00.450
That was Onbat!

03:02.230 --> 03:02.900
Luchabull!

03:04.910 --> 03:05.710
Everyone, return!

03:05.940 --> 03:06.550
You guys too!

03:06.850 --> 03:07.530
Return!

03:12.030 --> 03:13.080
Dedenne, Squishy!

03:27.950 --> 03:29.270
Onbat!

03:38.070 --> 03:39.600
Onbat, are you all right?

03:40.880 --> 03:42.510
It is showing symptoms of being poisoned!

03:43.730 --> 03:45.810
Could that Kinogassa we just saw have done this?

03:46.480 --> 03:47.630
I wonder what happened.

03:48.240 --> 03:50.080
Hey, Citron, can you treat it?

03:50.870 --> 03:54.510
The thing is, we are out of Antidote right now.

03:55.300 --> 03:56.580
We have no Momon Berries either...

03:56.910 --> 03:57.580
What?!

03:57.950 --> 03:59.600
What shall we do then?

04:12.530 --> 04:13.450
A Floette!

04:23.430 --> 04:25.450
Could this be...?

04:28.070 --> 04:29.950
Floette, the Single Flower Pokémon.

04:30.530 --> 04:37.330
It flutters around fields of flowers and cares for flowers that are starting to wilt. It is capable of drawing out the power of flowers.

04:38.500 --> 04:39.760
That is Aromatherapy!

04:40.390 --> 04:42.850
It cures a Pokémon's status condition.

04:47.390 --> 04:48.340
Onbat!

04:50.030 --> 04:52.270
Thank you, Floette. You saved it.

04:58.770 --> 05:00.900
Hmm... A Floette, huh?

05:01.390 --> 05:04.960
It's perfect as a foil for Pumpjin at Tripokalons.

05:06.160 --> 05:09.670
I rather think <i>Pumpjin</i> will be the foil.

05:09.670 --> 05:12.400
Floette-chan is so much cuter, after all.

05:13.680 --> 05:15.150
You think it's cute, huh?

05:15.590 --> 05:17.710
Uh, hey, Pumpjin-chan is cuter!

05:18.080 --> 05:18.630
Let's go!

05:21.520 --> 05:27.120
It says that once a year, this entire area gets filled with Floette that come riding the seasonal winds.

05:27.620 --> 05:28.430
Wow...

05:28.910 --> 05:30.710
But this little one seems to be on its own.

05:37.280 --> 05:38.210
Onbat!

06:10.960 --> 06:13.630
Onbat seems to be having lots of fun!

06:14.820 --> 06:16.270
They must be compatible.

06:16.660 --> 06:23.200
In terms of type compatibility, a Dragon type like Onbat should have a disadvantage against a Fairy type like Floette.

06:23.590 --> 06:25.360
You're so thick, bro.

06:39.680 --> 06:41.110
It is the gang from earlier!

06:44.070 --> 06:45.760
Kinogassa, the Mushroom Pokémon.

06:46.300 --> 06:51.550
It scatters poisonous spores and throws powerful punches while its foe is hampered by inhaled spores.

06:54.310 --> 06:55.460
What is it trying to do?

07:05.190 --> 07:05.890
Those guys...!

07:25.630 --> 07:27.150
I wonder what they're trying to do?

07:27.870 --> 07:30.800
Does Kinogassa like Floette?

07:30.800 --> 07:31.120
Huh?

07:37.890 --> 07:42.140
It must have disliked how well Onbat and Floette got along.

07:50.030 --> 07:52.610
But Floette doesn't want the attention.

07:59.710 --> 08:00.550
Onbat?

08:02.480 --> 08:04.850
I see. You want to help it!

08:06.930 --> 08:08.740
All right, go for it, Onbat!

08:14.260 --> 08:15.460
Onbat, don't give up!

08:26.990 --> 08:28.370
Are you all right, Onbat?

08:57.060 --> 08:59.680
So it is a one-on-one showdown.

09:00.340 --> 09:02.480
But Satoshi, at this rate...

09:03.200 --> 09:04.080
Make them stop.

09:04.660 --> 09:05.340
No.

09:06.230 --> 09:07.790
Onbat is saying that wants to do this.

09:17.110 --> 09:17.860
Onbat!

09:29.840 --> 09:31.390
Are you all right, Onbat?

09:37.620 --> 09:38.720
As Luchabull says,

09:39.140 --> 09:41.620
they've decided this is going to be a fight between two men.

09:43.840 --> 09:45.560
We can leave this to Onbat.

09:49.910 --> 09:50.610
Isn't that right,

09:51.140 --> 09:52.020
Onbat?

09:56.420 --> 09:57.990
That's what makes you a man!

10:02.830 --> 10:05.090
Why is the brat boy so fired up?

10:06.100 --> 10:07.730
He's a man.

10:07.730 --> 10:08.640
Yeah.

10:10.260 --> 10:12.290
I have no idea what's going on,

10:12.290 --> 10:13.110
but let's just put our plan in motion.

10:13.110 --> 10:13.840
Roger!

10:27.390 --> 10:28.180
Good job!

10:33.030 --> 10:33.890
All right!

10:41.890 --> 10:42.610
Onbat!

10:42.950 --> 10:43.710
At this rate...

10:43.710 --> 10:45.570
It's gonna beat up Onbat!

11:04.500 --> 11:05.230
What's going on?!

11:07.630 --> 11:09.750
If you say "What's going on?",

11:10.020 --> 11:12.060
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

11:12.740 --> 11:14.560
To prevent the world's destruction!

11:15.150 --> 11:17.390
To protect the world's peace!

11:17.680 --> 11:20.290
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

11:20.770 --> 11:23.070
we're lovely, charmy villains!

11:24.210 --> 11:24.900
Musashi!

11:25.350 --> 11:25.620
Kojiro!

11:26.230 --> 11:28.990
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

11:29.190 --> 11:32.110
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

11:32.110 --> 11:33.540
Just kidding!

11:37.360 --> 11:38.290
Rocket Gang!

11:39.270 --> 11:40.960
We've got some unnecessary cargo, but...

11:40.960 --> 11:43.430
...Floette-chan is ours now!

11:45.190 --> 11:46.990
Our plan was a huge success!

11:50.150 --> 11:51.870
Bye!

11:52.980 --> 11:54.270
Whoa!

11:58.880 --> 11:59.650
They got away...

12:06.050 --> 12:07.030
Pokémon Quiz!

12:07.410 --> 12:08.000
The answer...

12:08.000 --> 12:08.660
...is...

12:08.660 --> 12:09.140
...what?

12:22.510 --> 12:25.050
Don't worry. Leave this to us.

12:27.090 --> 12:29.280
First off, bro, it's time for one of your beloved machines.

12:29.890 --> 12:33.480
Heh heh heh... It is time for science to open up the future!

12:33.950 --> 12:35.510
Citronic Gear on!

12:36.070 --> 12:39.380
I envisioned a situation like this and prepared a nice machine!

12:39.590 --> 12:41.990
I call it the Aroma Sensing Machine!

12:42.470 --> 12:45.940
This is a groundbreaking machine that senses the aroma emitted by a Pokémon's flower.

12:46.530 --> 12:48.490
Please don't make it go boom, okay?

12:48.710 --> 12:50.180
I am confident in my work!

12:50.180 --> 12:51.410
Please watch.

12:51.600 --> 12:52.450
Switch on!

12:58.470 --> 12:59.980
It has sensed its aroma!

12:59.980 --> 13:02.500
Wow! Technology is amazing!

13:03.620 --> 13:04.690
This way.

13:05.070 --> 13:06.630
I can see why you're confident in it.

13:07.120 --> 13:07.940
Spear, you guys come too!

13:16.870 --> 13:18.020
Cheers!

13:20.530 --> 13:22.610
Woah, that went well!

13:22.820 --> 13:24.740
Our plan was a huge success.

13:25.070 --> 13:30.260
But see... Now comes the part where we always get overconfident and fail.

13:30.690 --> 13:35.540
Don't be so stuffy. We'll think about that if we <i>do</i> fail.

13:37.120 --> 13:38.840
Life's only worth living if you live it!

13:39.270 --> 13:40.740
You've got a point there!

13:54.070 --> 13:55.990
Bro, are we there yet?

13:57.200 --> 13:59.310
We should be close by now...

14:02.750 --> 14:04.530
Huh? Huh? Huh?!

14:03.790 --> 14:06.040
Bro, what did I say about not making it go boom...?

14:08.830 --> 14:10.510
I knew this would happen...

14:10.750 --> 14:11.410
Cough...

14:12.820 --> 14:13.710
If we're close...

14:14.270 --> 14:14.950
Onbat!

14:21.970 --> 14:24.230
I see! It is going to look for them with its Supersonic!

14:24.510 --> 14:25.870
We will count on you, Onbat!

14:28.670 --> 14:30.000
Do your best!

14:34.240 --> 14:35.090
Did you find it out?

14:37.570 --> 14:38.500
All right, let's go!

14:38.820 --> 14:39.120
Yeah.

14:41.220 --> 14:43.310
I've got Pumpjin and Nyarth, right?

14:43.620 --> 14:46.230
Then the pair of Sonansu and Floette!

14:46.630 --> 14:48.720
With them, I'll win Tripokalons!

14:48.910 --> 14:51.150
And it'll be decided that I'm Kalos Queen!

14:51.410 --> 14:55.150
If that happens, I'll be so popular with the Pokémon ladies of Kalos!

14:57.280 --> 15:01.370
If we get them all and hand them over to Sakaki-sama...

15:03.490 --> 15:06.470
Somehow, this feels <i>really</i> good!

15:09.600 --> 15:10.500
Whoa!

15:12.290 --> 15:14.610
You're too early!

15:15.380 --> 15:17.250
We won't let you get away any more, Rocket Gang!

15:17.470 --> 15:19.360
Let Floette and Kinogassa go!

15:20.590 --> 15:24.270
Geez! Let us bask in the afterglow of our victory a little!

15:26.110 --> 15:27.350
Now, go!

15:27.680 --> 15:28.850
Maaiika!

15:32.110 --> 15:33.110
Psybeam!

15:41.670 --> 15:43.490
Leave the Rocket Gang to us!

15:43.780 --> 15:45.310
Onbat, you take care of Floette!

15:47.780 --> 15:48.610
I'll go too!

15:49.270 --> 15:51.280
How arrogant of you.

15:51.840 --> 15:53.510
Pumpjin, Seed Bomb!

15:53.730 --> 15:55.010
Go!

15:59.140 --> 16:00.640
Pikachu, Electro Ball!

16:06.290 --> 16:08.080
Luchabull, X-Scissor!

16:13.860 --> 16:15.070
Psybeam!

16:16.640 --> 16:17.740
Rentorar, please!

16:22.390 --> 16:23.200
Swift!

16:27.350 --> 16:27.880
What?!

16:41.630 --> 16:42.310
Onbat!

16:43.140 --> 16:44.770
It's no use, it won't break.

16:54.130 --> 16:55.920
Onbat, don't give up!

16:56.290 --> 16:58.850
You can do it. You want to save it, right?

17:09.350 --> 17:14.160
Onbat, if you keep going <i>you'll</i> break before the cage does!

17:16.370 --> 17:17.230
Onbat!

17:22.030 --> 17:22.560
That's...

17:23.170 --> 17:24.310
...Acrobatics!

17:24.720 --> 17:26.180
Oh, so it's a new move!

17:36.150 --> 17:37.250
All right!

17:48.160 --> 17:50.560
Let's have Pumpjin and Maaiika do a double attack!

17:50.560 --> 17:51.300
Okay!

17:55.570 --> 17:57.350
All right, use Acrobatics!

18:13.050 --> 18:15.460
This feels bad!

18:19.870 --> 18:20.980
Onbat!

18:22.190 --> 18:23.200
You did it!

18:54.340 --> 18:55.730
They're fighting again...

18:56.070 --> 18:57.590
They haven't learned their lesson, huh?

19:10.270 --> 19:11.540
Oh, look at that!

19:19.310 --> 19:20.910
That is what you were talking about earlier, Serena...

19:21.380 --> 19:24.560
Yeah, the Floette that come riding the seasonal winds.

19:25.510 --> 19:27.600
Be careful on your future journey!

19:29.540 --> 19:30.630
Take care!

19:30.820 --> 19:32.300
See you!

19:49.310 --> 19:51.330
I wonder how far they'll go, riding the wind.

19:51.590 --> 19:53.620
It must be to a lovely place.

19:55.140 --> 19:57.270
All right, we should set off too!

19:57.620 --> 19:58.750
Yeah!

20:02.260 --> 20:09.550
Seeing off the Floette that set off riding the wind, Satoshi and his friends also continue <i>their</i> journey.

20:10.440 --> 20:11.470
To be continued.

20:16.040 --> 20:21.050
Sunday January 24th at 8am!

20:18.590 --> 20:20.130
Pokénchi gets covered in flour!

20:23.890 --> 20:26.110
Hot-blooded Pokémon Challenge!!

20:26.850 --> 20:29.550
The program that passionately presents Pokémon battles.

20:29.940 --> 20:32.370
Today we'll introduce Luchabull to you.

20:33.360 --> 20:35.320
Look at this Karate Chop...

20:35.600 --> 20:37.570
...leading into a High Jump Kick!

20:38.150 --> 20:39.780
That's a fluid combination.

20:40.150 --> 20:41.830
Dark Luchabull isn't falling behind either!

20:42.350 --> 20:46.370
Such passion! This is what I call a fight between men!

20:47.200 --> 20:50.150
Wow! Dark Luchabull is knocked down!

20:51.390 --> 20:52.720
Both of you did a good job.

20:53.200 --> 20:55.100
Luchabull, Dark Luchabull,

20:55.600 --> 20:56.960
thanks for this moving show!

20:57.890 --> 21:01.490
What enables it to fight like that is daily training, such as what we see here.

21:10.100 --> 21:11.870
And sometimes, this happens.

21:12.690 --> 21:14.690
But don't lose heart, Luchabull!

21:18.270 --> 21:20.210
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.400 --> 21:21.490
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.740 --> 21:26.000
Pierre-san from the Tripokalons is hosting a dance party!

21:26.150 --> 21:29.330
Since Elle-san will be one of the guests, I <i>have</i> to participate!

21:29.730 --> 21:31.250
Let's see, to participate...

21:31.550 --> 21:34.320
...the Pokémon and the Trainers need to come in pairs of one male and one female...

21:35.200 --> 21:36.050
What?!

21:37.140 --> 21:39.650
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:40.070 --> 21:42.660
Satoshi and Serena! Getting One at a Dance Party!!

21:42.600 --> 21:46.090
Next Time

21:42.600 --> 21:46.090
Satoshi and Serena!
Getting One at a Dance Party!!

21:43.280 --> 21:45.040
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:46.130 --> 21:56.100
Next episode:

21:46.130 --> 21:51.090
Everyone participates in a dance party!

21:46.930 --> 21:51.510
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

21:51.120 --> 21:56.100
Satoshi and Serena end up...!?
